 "poem": "Glared gleam from the lurid debris\nOf gods that writhed o'er eternity\nLike a black dog at celebration,\nAnd smelt the heaped corpse of a incarnation.\nShone in a blaze, and on debris\nBlazed as for murder; shone upon me\nIn my victory over temptation;\nBut it was not fear or consternation.\nBut it was silence, contemplation,\nAnd I turned from thought to inspiration,\nFor I saw there no cloud in my contemplation.\nAt last I felt myself borne out someone,",
